// Error pressure is LEVEL-ANCHORED: ERROR records always count; WARN
// records count only when they carry a provider-failure token (the retry-
// loop shape · the Class-C fingerprint was ProviderHeaderTimeoutError x182).
// Bare token mentions (INFO retry chatter, stack-trace continuation lines)
// never count: a slow-but-progressing max-reasoning step can legitimately
// outlast the spin window with a few recovered transients. Proxy-observed
// failures are the second pressure source (see the proxy-log loop).
// opencode >= 1.16 writes structured logfmt: "timestamp=... level=ERROR
// run=... message=...". The level is NOT at line start, so a /^ERROR/
// anchor matches nothing and errsSinceProgress stays 0 for the whole run ·
// the spin kill then can never fire from opencode's own log (observed on
// every Inkling xhigh trial 2026-07-26: 200+ level=ERROR lines, 179 probes
// all reporting errs_since_progress 0). Accept both shapes, and ONLY those
// two: a bare `\sERROR\b` alternative would also match the word inside an
// INFO record's message text (level=INFO ... message="tool exited with
// ERROR"), and 8 of those inside the spin window SIGTERM a healthy agent.
const ERROR_LINE = /^\s*ERROR\b|\blevel=ERROR\b/;
const WARN_LINE = /^\s*(WARN|WARNING)\b|\blevel=(WARN|WARNING)\b/;
const ERROR_TOKEN = /ProviderHeaderTimeoutError|AbortError|APICallError|FetchError|ECONNRESET|ETIMEDOUT/;
